# Spendly ERD — Mermaid source

The ERD is split into bounded diagrams for readability. `||--o{` means one-to-many; `}o--o{` indicates many-to-many resolved by an associative entity.

## 1. Identity, household and spaces

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ SESSIONS : authenticates
    USERS ||--|| USER_PREFERENCES : configures
    USERS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS : joins
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS : contains
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS : invites
    USERS ||--o{ HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS : creates
    USERS ||--o{ SPACES : owns_personal
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ SPACES : owns_shared

    USERS {
      uuid id PK
      string email_normalized UK
      string password_hash
      string status
      string primary_currency_code FK
      string timezone
    }
    SESSIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid user_id FK
      string token_hash UK
      datetime expires_at
      datetime revoked_at
    }
    USER_PREFERENCES {
      uuid user_id PK,FK
      string theme_key
      string communication_style
      string motion_level
      json notification_preferences
    }
    HOUSEHOLDS {
      uuid id PK
      string name
      uuid created_by_user_id FK
      string status
    }
    HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERSHIPS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid household_id FK
      uuid user_id FK
      string role
      string status
    }
    HOUSEHOLD_INVITATIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid household_id FK
      uuid created_by_user_id FK
      string token_hash UK
      datetime expires_at
      datetime revoked_at
    }
    SPACES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid owner_user_id FK
      uuid household_id FK
      string name
      string type
      string visibility_policy
    }
```

**Invariant:** `SPACES.owner_user_id` XOR `SPACES.household_id` — exactly one must be non-null.

## 2. Financial event, ledger and attribution

```mermaid
erDiagram
    CURRENCIES ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : denominates
    CURRENCIES ||--o{ FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS : denominates
    USERS ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : owns_personal
    HOUSEHOLDS ||--o{ ACCOUNTS : owns_shared
    ACCOUNTS ||--o{ ACCOUNT_ENTRIES : receives
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--|{ ACCOUNT_ENTRIES : posts
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : attributes
    SPACES ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : receives
    CATEGORIES ||--o{ TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS : classifies
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o| TRANSFER_DETAILS : describes_transfer
    ACCOUNT_ENTRIES ||--o| TRANSFER_DETAILS : source_entry

    CURRENCIES {
      string code PK
      string name
      string symbol
      int minor_unit_digits
    }
    ACCOUNTS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid owner_user_id FK
      uuid household_id FK
      string name
      string type
      string currency_code FK
      boolean include_in_safe_to_spend
      string status
    }
    CATEGORIES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid owner_user_id FK
      uuid household_id FK
      string name
      string kind
      boolean is_system_default
    }
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid created_by_user_id FK
      string transaction_type
      string status
      decimal amount
      string currency_code FK
      datetime occurred_at
      uuid original_transaction_id FK
    }
    ACCOUNT_ENTRIES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid transaction_id FK
      uuid account_id FK
      decimal amount_signed
      string currency_code FK
      string entry_role
    }
    TRANSACTION_ALLOCATIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid transaction_id FK
      uuid space_id FK
      uuid category_id FK
      uuid beneficiary_user_id FK
      decimal amount
      uuid reverses_allocation_id FK
    }
    TRANSFER_DETAILS {
      uuid transaction_id PK,FK
      uuid source_account_entry_id FK
      uuid destination_account_entry_id FK
    }
```

The transfer details row references both source and destination entries; the diagram shows the source relation explicitly to avoid clutter. Both entry IDs are foreign keys and unique.

## 3. Income forecasts and receipts

```mermaid
erDiagram
    INCOME_SOURCES ||--o{ INCOME_SCHEDULES : defines
    INCOME_SOURCES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : originates
    INCOME_SCHEDULES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : forecasts
    SPACES ||--o{ INCOME_SCHEDULES : scopes
    SPACES ||--o{ INCOME_OCCURRENCES : scopes
    INCOME_OCCURRENCES ||--o{ INCOME_RECEIPTS : reconciles
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ INCOME_RECEIPTS : records_actual_receipt

    INCOME_SOURCES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid owner_user_id FK
      string name
      string source_type
      string status
    }
    INCOME_SCHEDULES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid income_source_id FK
      uuid space_id FK
      decimal expected_amount
      string currency_code
      string frequency_type
      string recurrence_rule
      date expected_next_date
    }
    INCOME_OCCURRENCES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid income_schedule_id FK
      uuid income_source_id FK
      uuid space_id FK
      decimal expected_amount
      string currency_code
      date expected_date
      string status
    }
    INCOME_RECEIPTS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid income_occurrence_id FK
      uuid transaction_id FK
      decimal received_amount
      datetime received_at
    }
```

Expected occurrences do not create account entries. Actual receipt transactions do.

## 4. Budgets, commitments, goals and reserves

```mermaid
erDiagram
    SPACES ||--o{ BUDGET_PLANS : owns
    BUDGET_PLANS ||--o{ BUDGET_PERIODS : instantiates
    BUDGET_PERIODS ||--o{ BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS : plans
    CATEGORIES ||--o{ BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS : classifies
    SPACES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES : owns
    COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES : generates
    SPACES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES : scopes
    COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES ||--o{ COMMITMENT_PAYMENTS : paid_by
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ COMMITMENT_PAYMENTS : actual_payment
    SPACES ||--o{ GOALS : owns
    GOALS ||--o{ GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS : tracks
    GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS ||--o| FUND_RESERVATIONS : earmarks
    ACCOUNTS ||--o{ FUND_RESERVATIONS : reserves_from
    FINANCIAL_TRANSACTIONS ||--o{ GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS : transfer_link

    BUDGET_PLANS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid space_id FK
      string name
      string currency_code
      string period_type
      string status
    }
    BUDGET_PERIODS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid budget_plan_id FK
      date period_start
      date period_end
      string status
    }
    BUDGET_ALLOCATIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid budget_period_id FK
      uuid category_id FK
      decimal planned_amount
    }
    COMMITMENT_TEMPLATES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid space_id FK
      string name
      decimal expected_amount
      string currency_code
      string recurrence_rule
    }
    COMMITMENT_OCCURRENCES {
      uuid id PK
      uuid commitment_template_id FK
      uuid space_id FK
      decimal expected_amount
      string currency_code
      date due_date
      string status
    }
    COMMITMENT_PAYMENTS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid commitment_occurrence_id FK
      uuid transaction_id FK
      decimal applied_amount
    }
    GOALS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid space_id FK
      string name
      decimal target_amount
      string currency_code
      date target_date
    }
    GOAL_CONTRIBUTIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid goal_id FK
      string contribution_type
      decimal amount
      uuid fund_reservation_id FK
      uuid transfer_transaction_id FK
    }
    FUND_RESERVATIONS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid account_id FK
      decimal amount
      string currency_code
      string reservation_type
      string status
    }
```

## 5. Reliability and history

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ IDEMPOTENCY_RECORDS : submits
    USERS ||--o{ AUDIT_EVENTS : acts
    CURRENCIES ||--o{ FX_RATES : base_currency

    IDEMPOTENCY_RECORDS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid user_id FK
      string operation_scope
      string idempotency_key
      string request_hash
    }
    AUDIT_EVENTS {
      uuid id PK
      uuid actor_user_id FK
      string action
      string resource_type
      uuid resource_id
      datetime occurred_at
    }
    FX_RATES {
      uuid id PK
      string base_currency_code FK
      string quote_currency_code FK
      decimal rate
      string rate_source
      datetime rate_timestamp
    }
```
